                        ],
                        "form": "распыли́в"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "c7483bc7-cbce-402f-b83b-d1092cbde543",
                        "entry_id": "4cf72fa6-7aeb-3f73-b385-93e487adbd64",
                        "tags": [
                            "adverbial",
                            "participle",
                            "past"
                        ],
                        "form": "распыли́вши"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5d8b08c2-c806-36e4-9f98-65f2e66c9f7e",
                        "entry_id": "4cf72fa6-7aeb-3f73-b385-93e487adbd64",
                        "glosses": [
                            "измельчить, обратить в пыль"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "что."
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1d18db23-8929-4855-aab9-74592e3956ef",
                                "sense_id": "5d8b08c2-c806-36e4-9f98-65f2e66c9f7e",
                                "text": "Он живёт тысячи лет, солнце высушило его тело, кровь и кости, и ветер распылил их."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2f0215b3-5065-3691-ad55-fff58352099b",
                        "entry_id": "4cf72fa6-7aeb-3f73-b385-93e487adbd64",
                        "glosses": [
                            "рассеять жидкость, порошок, превратив в облако мелких пылевидных частиц"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e11f9de3-338b-4e04-9829-6c39aecaafb5",
                                "sense_id": "2f0215b3-5065-3691-ad55-fff58352099b",
                                "text": "Напомню, что американская ракета «Сатурн» распылила в 1961 году 86 тонн воды на высоту от 100 до 150 километров — вне озоносферы и, судя по времени запуска (октябрь), не в самое благоприятное для гидратообразования по температурным условиям время."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "da69d45a-236c-4203-9cad-c6f4fb688399",
                                "sense_id": "2f0215b3-5065-3691-ad55-fff58352099b",
                                "text": "Моё двухкомнатное жильё хранило запах пищи ушедших поколений, и я в безрассудной надежде распылил пару баллончиков дезодоранта."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1cec6a03-d1cd-3f77-bef8-3f1c3626a600",
                        "entry_id": "4cf72fa6-7aeb-3f73-b385-93e487adbd64",
                        "glosses": [
                            "перен. рассеять, рассредоточить, лишая этим действенности, силы"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "кого-что."
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a7deebaf-1f92-43cc-b516-dfb4d49612ff",
                                "sense_id": "1cec6a03-d1cd-3f77-bef8-3f1c3626a600",
                                "text": "Революцию распылили… Революцию истощили… Теперь фонд живых сил революции истощён."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f7e6aaac-6c21-45ae-984a-60216b9d95fc",
                                "sense_id": "1cec6a03-d1cd-3f77-bef8-3f1c3626a600",
                                "text": "Боясь присутствия русской вооружённой силы, они по предписанию из Парижа и Лондона старались всячески распылить армию и трактовали её как беженскую массу."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "01c11d6c-9ee6-41dc-a174-693d3f91ce8f",
                        "source_entry_id": "4cf72fa6-7aeb-3f73-b385-93e487adbd64",
                        "source_sense_description": "измельчить, обратить в пыль",
                        "target_lang_word": "turn to dust",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "turn to dust",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0849e136-0429-3e3c-9cef-f34c5472c664",
                                        "entry_id": "83e928ca-4ccb-3953-a90c-5b61b88bf679",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To die or disappear."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "idiomatic",
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "43143e92-fc89-4dc4-a1de-30a2df941d23",
                                                "sense_id": "0849e136-0429-3e3c-9cef-f34c5472c664",
                                                "text": "If I lost my dreams\nCould I keep your trust\nPromise that our love\nWould not turn to dust"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "168e7389-1d66-4ad0-832c-87b17af4df19",
                                                "sense_id": "0849e136-0429-3e3c-9cef-f34c5472c664",
                                                "text": "Now he threatens to walk away from Ukraine altogether, impatient to get a deal in time for his 100th-day celebrations on Tuesday. That’s typical too: so often Trump’s grand plans turn to dust because, if he doesn’t get an instant reward, he gets bored and drifts away."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b405518c-10f4-49d2-8e88-ef3310606bf8",
                        "source_entry_id": "4cf72fa6-7aeb-3f73-b385-93e487adbd64",
                        "source_sense_description": "рассеять жидкость, порошок, превратив в облако мелких пылевидных частиц",
                        "target_lang_word": "dispel",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "dispel",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5dbee63c-e9d2-3ce1-ad63-11b75743f4d1",
                                        "entry_id": "d5195e05-5ecf-3649-a561-1a86400d70bc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To drive away or cause to vanish by scattering."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "83e80f9c-fb4a-4249-9e18-43ccb17c1938",
                                                "sense_id": "5dbee63c-e9d2-3ce1-ad63-11b75743f4d1",
                                                "text": "The clouds and mist were soon enough dispelled by the sun."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "34ed9f94-627a-3568-a77b-90d64c8e0b2f",
                                        "entry_id": "d5195e05-5ecf-3649-a561-1a86400d70bc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To remove (fears, doubts, objections etc.) by proving them unjustified."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d7471383-090b-436a-9dd0-1e313124c34d",
                                                "sense_id": "34ed9f94-627a-3568-a77b-90d64c8e0b2f",
                                                "text": "It was April 22, 1831, and a young man was walking down Whitehall in the direction of Parliament Street.[…]. He halted opposite the Privy Gardens, and, with his face turned skywards, listened until the sound of the Tower guns smote again on the ear and dispelled his doubts."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f9e706b1-a9b2-4c2e-95d1-8e732e80407e",
                                                "sense_id": "34ed9f94-627a-3568-a77b-90d64c8e0b2f",
                                                "text": "The fate of the railway from Ballater to Braemar has been invested with an air of mystery, which has never been completely dispelled. It has been suggested that Queen Victoria was opposed to a railway in the vicinity of Balmoral Castle, and intervened personally to secure the abandonment of the line beyond Ballater."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "dispel",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "43a799ad-be58-3837-988d-4205cf69ff79",
                                        "entry_id": "fd72be32-5f01-377f-96ce-f7cfe5d35711",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An act or instance of dispelling."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a81a79f1-0cf6-42d8-a2a4-9c4d8e960e9a",
                                                "sense_id": "43a799ad-be58-3837-988d-4205cf69ff79",
                                                "text": "“My dispel didn't work,” she said finally. “He wasn't a blood witch, Sunny,” I said."
                                            }
                                        ]
